# Template for .confidential-patterns (which is gitignored — never commit the real one).
#
#   cp .confidential-patterns.example .confidential-patterns
#   # then add your real firm / product / person / account identifiers below
#
# scripts/check-no-secrets.sh loads .confidential-patterns and blocks a push if any
# of these regexes match the committed tree. One POSIX extended-regex per line;
# matched case-insensitively. Blank lines and # comments are ignored. The real file
# stays local so the committed gate never leaks the names it guards against.
#
# Replace the placeholders below with your own; delete the ones you do not need.

# Firm / brand
# my-company
# \bmybrand\b

# Products / project codenames
# \bmyproduct\b
# project-codename

# Accounts / handles / refs
# my-github-org
# my-team\.internal\.example\.com
# [a-z0-9]{20}          # e.g. a database/project ref from your .env

# People (real individuals)
# \b(alice|bob|carol)\b
# surname
